                        "sense_id": "e9b9d79a-3662-386f-aaf2-5c58a2c80cfe",
                        "entry_id": "eaea42d2-e153-36a1-9f40-b3e519bf18fb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A primordium, the initial clustering of embryonic cells from which a body part develops."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed01856d-ef89-4a7f-a08c-225e94e7da03",
                                "sense_id": "e9b9d79a-3662-386f-aaf2-5c58a2c80cfe",
                                "text": "Stockard has shown that, not only do anesthetics arrest the development of the intra-embryonic blood vessels in the embryos of Fundulus, at an early ontogenetic stage, but in such a manner that no doubt can now exist that, under normal conditions, these vessels are formed in situ by a concrescence of independent and discontinuous anlagen, and that their endothelium is derived directly from intra-embryonic mesenchymal cells."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16454001-92f8-466c-b7ec-643a4ad69f3e",
                                "sense_id": "e9b9d79a-3662-386f-aaf2-5c58a2c80cfe",
                                "text": "Moreover, most species have a cirral pattern which - at least partially - closely resembles that of 18-cirri hypotrichs, including the formation from six (I-VI) anlagen."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "26231d9f-193b-32a2-abed-ecb36c912c06",
